WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
In Sikh tradition, a
Mughal emperor, Akbar,

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.790
once sat on the floor to eat.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.750
He ate the same free
food, in the same rows,

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.420
as everyone else.

5
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:17.000
Over a century later, in 1705, a Sikh
woman named Mai Bhago led forty soldiers

6
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.580
back into battle.

7
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.310
Why did she lead them back?

8
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.510
And what did it prove to Sikhs?

9
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.210
In this mission, you'll read what
Guru Nanak taught about caste,

10
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.720
and about women.

11
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.140
Then you'll weigh up whether Sikhs
today fully live out that teaching.

12
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.540
Your mission: find out
why Mai Bhago matters,

13
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.800
and what equality means for Sikhs.
